<title>INDIA: Indian exports rose 1.15 percent in February.</title>
<headline>Indian exports rose 1.15 percent in February.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to $2.65 billion in February, up 1.15 percent from $2.62 billion in the same month in 1996, the government said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.65	2.84	2.62</p>
<p>    Imports		  3.55	3.75	2.80</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.90     -0.91     -0.18</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports totalled $29.80 billion between April 1996 and February 1997, up 5.61 percent from $28.22 billion in April 1995 to February 1996, the statement said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Apr 96-Feb 97    Apr 95-Feb 96</p>
<p>    Exports		     29.80		28.22</p>
<p>    Imports		     35.06		32.52</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -5.26		-4.30</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
